{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/929665-ordo-dracul-kogaions-in-the-second-edition","id":929665,"title":"Ordo Dracul Kogaions in the Second Edition","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-11T05:18:19-07:00","id":929665,"title":"Ordo Dracul Kogaions in the Second Edition","content":"Hey all . <br /> <br /> Due to Secrets of the Covenants not out yet and the book being very brief in the Covenants Section.<br /> <br /> It is mentioned that the position of Kogaion is a burden for ordo Elders and they are a chore.<br /> <br /> The Merit Sworn of Mysteries mentions that they are the political part of the Covenant and other Ordo defer to them . <br /> <br /> How you play this interaction and the position of the Kogaion in the Covenant . Is it a more hands off position ? Is it near the Invictus rigid hierarchical structures? how the position of Kogaion interacts with the Sworn of Mysteries.<br /> <br /> In a political disagreement between these 2 and assuming they have equal status who wins?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for all your answers.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Member of the Requiem For Greece Storyteller Team<br /> <br /> City of Athens Storyteller<br /> <br /> Exalted funboy","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/823-balancer","name":"Balancer","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-11T07:30:30-07:00","id":929721,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Balancer</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/929665-ordo-dracul-kogaions-in-the-second-edition#post929665\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey all .<br /> <br /> Due to Secrets of the Covenants not out yet and the book being very brief in the Covenants Section.<br /> <br /> It is mentioned that the position of Kogaion is a burden for ordo Elders and they are a chore.<br /> <br /> The Merit Sworn of Mysteries mentions that they are the political part of the Covenant and other Ordo defer to them .<br /> <br /> How you play this interaction and the position of the Kogaion in the Covenant . Is it a more hands off position ? Is it near the Invictus rigid hierarchical structures? how the position of Kogaion interacts with the Sworn of Mysteries.<br /> <br /> In a political disagreement between these 2 and assuming they have equal status who wins?<br /> <br /> Thanks in advance for all your answers.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Ordo Dracul are structured like a secret society of occultists and quasi-scientists. Apart from the shame in admitting that one is an elder who has not yet transcended vampirism to such an extent so as to no longer need to interact with the Order (like Dracula supposedly did), a Kogaion suffers the same responsibilities a leading figure in any secret society does (just look for historical examples, such as the Rosicrucian, the Filiki, and Hermetic orders pre- and post-Crowley).<br /> <br /> Aside from their own Magnus Opum, which for a Dragon would be the mastery of one's dominant Mystery, a Kogaion is the go-to person for members of lower rank to present their progress, research, and new Scales. They definitely influence the standing of members in the Ordo Dracul's hierarchy (as per page 155 in V:tR 2nd edition). If they do not share in the burdensome task of mapping Wyrm's Nests, they at the very least partake in the organizing process: expeditions, researching a Wyrm's Nest history, as well as coming up with a plan for gaining access (if not controlling) the nest. They are likely to deal with intra-covenant interactions, which means they get dragged into boring political debates, contests, and outright conflicts, of little interest to a proper Dragon.<br /> <br /> Bottom line, think of the renowned college professor who may or may not enjoy teaching and interacting with her students. The very best, most approachable of them would rather carry on with their research than be in a classroom full of disciples who have still not mastered what the professor considers to be the very basics. Some particularly talented academics are notorious for being outspoken of their dislike for such interactions. I imagine a Kogaion to feel close to that example, and less towards the Invictus position of power and/or authority. Though, as with all things Requiem, YMMV. It wouldn't be unheard in the world of chronicles of darkness, for the Ordo Dracul of a particular city to base their rank and governing of the order around the model of a mystical order, an ancient Greek or Roman academy, a corporate R&amp;D facility, and so on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.greece-bynight.com\" target=\"_blank\">Greece By Night LARP</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/59-stylanski","name":"stylanski","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar59_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"299"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}